  F                   151.3899		Ratio of mean squares: the between-group mean square is 151.4 times the within-group mean square. With no real effect, this ratio tends to be near 1
  p                   < .001  (1.12e-25)		Statistically significant: if there were truly no effect, results at least this extreme would occur less than 0.1% of the time
  Effect size         eta-squared = 0.8973		Effect size: large by Cohen's convention (eta-squared >= 0.14 = large). Group membership accounts for 90% of the total variance
  Why: The ANOVA above pools one within-group spread across all groups. This checks whether that is a fair thing to do here.
  Equal spread        Brown-Forsythe F(3, 52) = 0.3362
  Equal-spread p      p = .799


